<title>BELGIUM: EU details intervention grain stocks.</title>
<headline>EU details intervention grain stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks of 1.93 million tonnes net consisted of the following varieties, European Commission figures showed.</p>
<p>The deadline for intervention offers was May 31, except in Sweden where an extra month is allowed.</p>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks (tonnes)</p>
<p>			 26/06/97	 12/6/97		   1/7/96</p>
<p> All cereals	1,934,695     1,828,578		2,596,112</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p> Soft wheat	   324,686	 346,598		  458,978</p>
<p> Durum wheat	    nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p> Barley		 616,616	 550,238		1,343,870</p>
<p> Rye		    990,863	 929,367		  793,261</p>
<p> Maize		    2,530	   2,375			  3</p>
<p> Sorghum		  nil	     nil		    nil</p>
<p> Triticale		nil	     nil		    nil</p>
<p>NB: Figures are net after deduction of domestic and export sales commitments</p>
</text>
